  "cause": "Collector unknown-A6 fallback excluded numeric custom-register offsets; renderer could name those same operands from declared app regions. Native low-field references were omitted. Partial extents and hardware-relative inputs could also be misleadingly named.",
  "implementation": {
    "shared_admission": "Known register/layout state, known hardware exclusions and explicitly labelled A6/layout fallbacks; decode-native operands/roles, no source-text reverse parsing.",
    "full_width_scope": "Canonical app region must cover decoded data width (or1byte for address-only use) to disambiguate a custom-offset collision. This is not a complete bulk/sparse footprint proof.",
    "hardware_transfer": "Reuse existing bounded low-WORD relative hardware domain in linear collector/render walks; KB-resolved full LEA/immediate hardware addresses retain base+offset. Reads, overwrites, calls and terminal linear flow do not manufacture a base.",
    "evidence_field": "Analysis and listing app_slot_refs.base_evidence distinguish register_state/use_site_binding/library_extension/a6_fallback/declared_layout_a6_fallback/unspecified. Fallbacks remain assumptions, not independently proved addresses or binding evidence IDs.",
    "scope": "Amiga lookup pass; no target-specific offsets in admission or instruction-size transformations."
  },
